  "body": "### What is the issue with the URL Standard?\n\n[The definition for a URL path](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-path) currently says \"A URL path is either a URL path segment or a list of zero or more URL path segments.\", but it's not clear if it's possible to have a segmented path with zero segments or if this case only occurs when starting to parse the path.\n\nIn particular I'm not clear if `non-special://host` has an empty opaque path or an empty segmented path.\n\nI think updating the table just above the URL path definition to include `non-special://host` would be enough, though I think requiring segmented paths to have at least one segment would be good. Just not sure how to rewrite the parser to account for that.",
